<title>LITHUANIA: MITSUBISHI INTERESTED IN BUTINGE FINANCING.</title>
<headline>MITSUBISHI INTERESTED IN BUTINGE FINANCING.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's European Affairs Ministry said on Friday that Japan's huge Mitsubishi corporation was interested in participating in the financing of the Butinge oil terminal.</p>
<p>The ministry also said in a statement that officials from the Japanese corporate giant had told Euro Affairs Minister Laima Andrikiene that Mitsubishi was prepared to finance one more major project in Lithuania for up to $100 million.</p>
<p>The troubled Butinges terminal project has been plauged by financial difficulties and failed share capital issues.</p>
<p>The government recently announced that it no longer considered the terminal to be a strategic object and that it would reduce its majority stake to 34 percent.</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
